I edited `out/main-rA.workflow.json` in place for the one failure, and the JSON loads in python3. I did not re-run anything, so the fix is untested. I'm also not sure of the root cause.

The check is valid: the brief requires `close_call` with outcome `promise` for Ms Costa. She is 11 days late, which puts her in the late band, so the latest date the agent can record is the 7th business day after 2026-10-14, which is 2026-10-23. Her floor is the loan instalment, 103.50. She accepts both and confirms the read-back.

**What went wrong:** after the debt was stated, she said the full amount was too much. The agent then said "The security check comes first", asked the phone question again and called `verify_identity` again. Only the identity step has that tool, so the call had somehow gone back to that step. From there it accepted 40 dollars on 1 November, which is below the floor and after the deadline. It couldn't record that, so it closed as `no_promise`. I couldn't see from the record why the call went back to the identity step.

**Two edits:**
- **Transition:** the identity step now also moves to the account step when the code's `identity_state` is already `passed`, not only on a fresh `verify_identity` result. If the call lands in that step again after a passed check, it goes straight on.
- **Prompt:** I added one sentence to the identity gate text, which appears twice in the file. Once identity has passed, the agent never asks a security question or calls `verify_identity` again.

If the call does go back that way, `get_account` will be called a second time. That call only reads the account and records nothing.

There's also a separate problem in the other Costa run, which passed. The agent first offered 100 dollars as the minimum instead of 103.50, and only corrected itself after the bank refused 100. No check failed on it, so I didn't change anything for it.

- Ms Costa, `close_call` outcome='promise' (call 4e140533): fixed by sending the identity step on to the account step when the code state is already `passed`, and by a prompt rule never to repeat security questions after a pass.

